---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import ContactClose from '../components/ContactClose.astro';
import { services } from '../data/services';
---
<Layout title="Cosmin Ghinoiu — Senior Client Delivery & Implementation Lead | Enterprise Software" description="Senior client delivery and implementation lead for enterprise software: implementations, migrations, service delivery and enterprise AI rollouts, mostly for pharma and life sciences. Open to permanent and contract roles and defined projects." current="/">
  <section class="home-intro">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <h1>Senior client delivery <br /><span>and implementation lead.</span></h1>
      <div class="intro-bottom">
        <div class="intro-copy">
          <p>I lead enterprise software delivery from requirements through launch and handover, and I stay with the client afterwards: onboarding and adoption, account and service reviews, escalations, integrations and the changes that come up once people are actually using the system. I coordinate clients, product, engineering and support teams, and I do a good part of the hands-on work myself, from data migration and configuration to training. It’s the same work whether the title says implementation, client delivery, service delivery or customer success.</p>
          <p class="intro-engagement">I’m open to permanent and contract roles, and to defined implementation projects.</p>
          <div class="button-row"><a class="button button-light" href="/contact/">Discuss a role <Arrow /></a><a class="text-link" href="/portfolio/">View portfolio <Arrow /></a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="intro-aside"><p>Most of my experience is with scientific-content platforms for global pharma and life-sciences organizations, including two enterprise AI rollouts delivered under content licensing constraints. Since October 2026 I also run SuppClaimCheck, a small production AI service of my own.</p><a href="/about/">Meet Cosmin <Arrow /></a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-proof intro-proof-grid">
        <p><strong>50+ specialized delivery projects</strong><span>Implementations, integrations, migrations, technical reviews and workflow redesigns, 2022 to July 2026, during employment.</span></p>
        <p><strong>5 strategic accounts, over $2M a year in licences</strong><span>Implementation and service manager for five enterprise SaaS accounts. Every account I managed renewed; contractual service levels met throughout.</span></p>
        <p><strong>Two enterprise AI rollouts</strong><span>A 12-month pilot that went to a launch for 20,000 users, and a second client’s AI search and summarization for its power users.</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="work-preview" aria-labelledby="work-title"><div class="section-wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="work-title">Selected delivery experience.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/portfolio/">View portfolio <Arrow /></a></div>
    <div class="project-list">
      <a class="project-row" href="/portfolio/#enterprise-rollout"><span>Enterprise AI delivery</span><h3>From pilot to a launch <br />for 20,000 users.</h3><p>I led a 12-month pilot across nine client workstreams and six internal teams, moved about 700,000 documents from the previous vendor in 40 days, and worked with the client and engineers on the evaluation and tuning that got the AI answers to where they needed to be. The user figure describes launch scope.</p><Arrow direction="up-right" /></a>
      <a class="project-row" href="/portfolio/#data-migration"><span>Hands-on implementation</span><h3>50,000+ documents. <br />25 configured libraries.</h3><p>I migrated documents and metadata into SaaS libraries, with responsibility for mapping, data quality, workflows and launch enablement.</p><Arrow direction="up-right" /></a>
      <a class="project-row" href="/portfolio/#account-consolidation"><span>Client delivery</span><h3>Three accounts. <br />One working setup.</h3><p>I led consolidation into a single 10,000-user account, coordinating around 30 stakeholders through full sign-off.</p><Arrow direction="up-right" /></a>
      <a class="project-row" href="/portfolio/#suppclaimcheck"><span>Independent AI project</span><h3>SuppClaimCheck: an AI service <br />I designed, direct and operate.</h3><p>Claude Code agents write the code under rules I set; I own the product, the evals, the security review, releases and operations. Verdict accuracy went from 47 to 53% to 75 to 81% across ten measured versions, inside a EUR 25 monthly budget.</p><Arrow direction="up-right" /></a>
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">The first three are work I delivered during employment, with clients anonymized; user figures describe launch or account scope, not measured active use. SuppClaimCheck is my own project, with the code written by AI coding agents under my direction.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="engagement section-wrap" aria-labelledby="engagement-title"><h2 id="engagement-title">Part of your team. <br />Or leading a defined project.</h2><div><p>In a permanent or contract role, I can take responsibility for client delivery, implementation, service delivery or customer success alongside the teams already involved.</p><p>For a defined project, the scope might be a migration, a difficult rollout, an AI pilot, or preparing users and operations for launch and handover.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Discuss a project <Arrow /></a></div></section>
  <section class="situations section-wrap" aria-labelledby="situations-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="situations-title">Where I can help.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/services/">Explore services <Arrow /></a></div>
    <div class="situation-list">
      {services.map((service) => <article class="situation"><div class="situation-main"><h3><a href={'/services/#' + service.id}>{service.title}<Arrow /></a></h3><p>{service.summary}</p></div><a class="evidence-link" href={service.href}><span>{service.proofTitle}</span><span class="evidence-action">Read the example <Arrow direction="up-right" /></span></a></article>)}
    </div>
  </section>
  <ContactClose />
</Layout>
